Code in this repository that looks borrowed, and is not

web/vendor/gifenc.js is under vendor/ because it is a self-contained encoder
with no imports, not because it came from somewhere else. It is a ~220-line
GIF89a/LZW writer written for this project and is covered by the Apache-2.0
licence above like the rest of the source. It shares a name with, but no code
with, the npm package `gifenc`.

web/bluenoise.json is data, not code: a 64x64 void-and-cluster threshold tile
generated by this project's own implementation (server/dither.py,
`blue_noise(64, 7)`), committed so that the browser and the server start from
identical noise. No third-party tile was used.

web/player/dither-player.js (the .dots.gz codec, the transitions and the
player) and server/cdither.c are likewise original to this project.

