Test media

docs/entry-clip.mp4 is trimmed from "View of a park while a girl runs across"
(https://mixkit.co/free-stock-video/view-of-a-park-while-a-girl-runs-across-4831/)
under the Mixkit Stock Video Free License
(https://mixkit.co/license/#videoFree). It is included solely as a test fixture
for the tracking verification suite. It is not part of the software and must not
be redistributed as a stock asset.

sample.mp4 is five seconds trimmed from "Man jumping from a wall"
(https://mixkit.co/free-stock-video/man-jumping-from-a-wall-21756/) under the
same licence, and sample.jpg is its first frame. They are the default inputs to
verify.mjs and verify-web.mjs, committed so that both suites run from a fresh
clone with no arguments. Same terms: test fixtures, not part of the software,
not redistributable as stock assets.

Any other clips or stills used while developing this project are test inputs
only and are not redistributed here.

web/demo/ holds the two files the page offers as a demo: sample.mp4 and
sample.jpg are copies of the root ones above and carry the same Mixkit terms,
clip-thumb.jpg and still-thumb.jpg are downscaled stills from them, and
demo.dots.gz is dot data produced from that clip by this project's own
pipeline. The screenshots under docs/ are frames of the same two clips as the
application renders them, kept as verification evidence.

